<title>UK: BP flares higher on gas supply deal.</title>
<headline>BP flares higher on gas supply deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum Plc were indicated 4p higher at 717-1/p by 0815 GMT after the oil and gas group said it had signed a 15-year agreement to supply gas valued at more than $1.0 billion, to Germany's Ruhrgas.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a long-term deal so in revenue terms it won't have a dramatic impact on revenues. But it is still a good deal for BP,&quot; the head of trading and sales at a large brokerage said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is hoping there will be similar deals in the future,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
